{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the fire</b> Three times in the Masorah: והאש על המזבח · והאש ירדה מן השמים · והאש תאכלם — hint to the one who says that Nadav and Avihu died because they ruled halakhah before their master and said: even though the fire descends from heaven, it is a mitzvah to bring from an ordinary person. And this: והאש ירדה מן השמים — even so, והאש תוקד בו, that one must bring from an ordinary person. Therefore מן האש יצאו — they ruled by fire, and the fire consumed them." "<b>And the fire upon the altar shall burn in it</b> — that it is like a ladder for angels to ascend, as it says (Judges 6:21): ויעל מלאך ה' בלהב המזבח. And likewise in Ezekiel: והנה ששה אנשים וגו' ויעמדו אצל מזבח הנחושת. Therefore it was of bronze, and they sparkled like the color of kalal bronze. But the inner altar corresponds to the Shekhinah, as written: ידיו גלילי זהב. Therefore any blood, if it entered inside — the sin offering is not eaten from it, for there is no eating above."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The third Masorah occurrence, והאש תאכלם, is not itself a phrase from Leviticus 6:5 but appears to be drawn from another verse; the Ba'al HaTurim cites it here as part of the Masorah juxtaposition.", 1 "Ezekiel citation reads והנה ששה אנשים וגו' as in Ezekiel 9:2; the full phrase including ויעמדו אצל מזבח הנחושת combines language from Ezekiel 9:2 and possibly 8:16."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:49.663047453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}